; HOLLOWREACH (Phase 38O) — the wharf down the water from Tarn's Landing, and the realm's FOURTH
; market. It is the only place in Embervale that will buy contraband, and that is the whole of its
; reason to exist: 38F built a system that prices a merchant's identity, and every merchant so far has
; been identified by what they DO sell. Sedge and Coyle are identified by what nobody else will.
;
; Hana the fishmonger has named this place since 38L, twelve sub-phases before it existed: "There's
; talk of the wharf down at Hollowreach selling cheaper. There's always talk. Cheaper fish usually
; means somebody didn't pay the toll." That line is now true, and it is the only signposting the
; district gets — there is no quest marker and no map pin until the waystone is found.
;
; ⚠️ NO NEW ART. Every model here was adopted for an earlier cell, and the wharf is built out of the
; Landing's kit re-read: the fishing hut is a harbourmaster's shed nobody mans, the ruined walls are a
; breakwater the sea took, and the watch tower stands over a wharf it has stopped watching. 38N2's
; retrospective spent an hour pulling an asset already on disk; this one spent none, because the
; library was checked first (manifest.json licence field, then `ls`) and it is genuinely out of
; unadopted medieval bodies — every CC0 character in it is already in assets/models/characters/.
;
; ⚠️ THE WATER IS A DECAL, NOT A VOLUME, and the lakebed under it is not decoration (38N2). A
; translucent plane with NO COLLIDER over a near-black skin: swimming does not exist, so a real water
; volume would be an invisible wall or a hole. The first pass at the Landing omitted the lakebed and
; the tarn read as flat grey ground, because a transparent surface needs something dark to be
; transparent against. That finding is carried here rather than re-earned.
;
; ⚠️ The jetties are sunk 0.30 m so their decks land flush. Their posts run below their own origin
; (jetty min.y = -1.05, dock min.y = -2.35 — measured off the written .glb, not the viewport), and a
; deck standing proud is a 34 cm kerb, which with no step-up on CharacterBody3D (38K) is an invisible
; wall across the one route to the water.
;
; ⚠️ Cell placed at Center (-106, 0, 74): a 52 m floor spanning x -132..-80, z 48..100. Tarn's Landing
; is the same x band ending at z 16, so the two share a coastline with 32 m of unbuilt water between
; them, and neither overlaps the Embermarket (x -26..26, z 20..72). A REGION LOADS WHOLE now, so this
; cell is permanently in the tree from the moment the Ember Crown is entered — the ninth.
;
; ⚠️ EVERYTHING STATIC PARENTS TO Nav; the two fences deliberately do not (only static geometry should
; carve the navmesh). Every transform is LOCAL.
;
; ⚠️ WHAT THE 2026-08-28 LAYOUT REBUILD REPLACED, AND ONE OF IT WAS A BUG. Four east-west bands — approach, shore road,
; wharf, water — with everything the district owns strung along one 44 m boardwalk, and a 20 m strip of
; lake down the whole western edge. It read as a diagram, and the road ran along z = 0 while the
; Embermarket's Dock Stair leaves the seam at world (-26, 58) — cell-local (26, 12) — so the two
; districts did not actually join on the ground.
;
; THE LAYOUT NOW — a street between two flooded channels, and a walled room off it:
;   x 6..26, z 8..16   THE STREET, in from the east at z = 12 where the Embermarket's stair arrives.
;                      The fallen colonnade, the waystone, the tents and the carts.
;   x 2..10, z 2..12   THE TURN, south around the head of the north channel.
;   x -16..6, z -6..8  THE SPINE — the strip of land the two channels leave between them. Fourteen
;                      metres wide, water on both sides, and the whole reason the district reads as
;                      drowned rather than as a jetty beside a lake.
;   x -14..-4, z -4..6 THE HOLLOW. Five ruin walls and two pillars make a chamber off the spine with
;                      one gap, on the SOUTH side, and no sightline from the street. Coyle's locker,
;                      two pitches and a brazier are inside it. Everything traded in Hollowreach is
;                      traded in a room you have to find.
;   x -26..6, z -14..-6   THE NORTH CHANNEL; x -26..2, z 8..18 THE SOUTH CHANNEL; x -26..-16 open
;                      water, with the Wet Hull at her berth and the jetties running out of the spine
;                      into both channels.
;   x 16..20, z -8     THE BONE TABLE, in a ruin north-east of the street. Nothing points at it.
;
; ⚠️ THE WATER IS SIX VISUAL BOXES AND HAS NO COLLIDER — Lakebed/Water plus the two channel pairs,
; parented OUTSIDE Nav at y = 0.02 / 0.05 over the same flat floor. The player can walk on it. That
; was true before this rebuild; it is greybox, not a regression.
;
; ⚠️ EVERYTHING STATIC PARENTS TO Nav. Geometry outside the NavigationRegion3D is not carved into the
; navmesh. The two fences deliberately do NOT enclose the Hollow — the ruin walls do, and a fence
; there would have read as a farmyard.

